            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Walter Raleigh</strong><br>\nWalter Raleigh was born around 1552 in Devon, England, into a well-connected family. His early life prepared him for a future as a courtier and explorer. He attended Oriel College, Oxford, before fighting for the Huguenots in the French religious civil wars. By the time he returned to England, Raleigh had developed the charismatic and adventurous spirit that would define his career.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Courtier to the Queen</strong><br>\nRaleigh's charm and wit soon caught the eye of Queen Elizabeth I, and he quickly rose in her favor. He became a gentleman of the queen's privy chamber and was knighted in 1585. Raleigh used his position to acquire patents and charters to explore and colonize the New World, which helped England establish its early overseas empire.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Virgin Queen's Favorite</strong><br>\nDespite not being a member of the nobility by birth, Raleigh became one of the most influential men in Elizabethan England. He was favored by Elizabeth I, who granted him extensive estates and trading privileges. His relationship with the queen allowed him a degree of power that was rare for someone of his origins, influencing political and economic decisions at the highest level.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
